                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6a122705-55ab-3146-835c-74ed274db74c",
                        "entry_id": "158e6575-269a-34aa-96e2-589309e4772e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To eat (parts of) another of one's own species."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "UK",
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "2086795e-44a9-4d63-8031-30ad48533b0d",
                                "sense_id": "6a122705-55ab-3146-835c-74ed274db74c",
                                "text": "The female black widow spider is known to cannibalise the male."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "50cba172-33c5-35ce-85d7-353f1917732d",
                        "entry_id": "158e6575-269a-34aa-96e2-589309e4772e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To remove parts of (a machine, etc) for use in other similar machines."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "UK",
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5d0ccfcc-fbf6-46f5-b796-3b417d0ac037",
                                "sense_id": "50cba172-33c5-35ce-85d7-353f1917732d",
                                "text": "to cannibalize an old laptop for parts"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9bf13a7e-07b5-4637-9efb-624b1de37367",
                                "sense_id": "50cba172-33c5-35ce-85d7-353f1917732d",
                                "text": "According to our correspondent, at least one of the Type 2s has had to be cannibalised to facilitate repairs, as spares are often in short supply."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8d840cde-2c62-4672-946a-aa9aacc78b68",
                                "sense_id": "50cba172-33c5-35ce-85d7-353f1917732d",
                                "text": "When the attack ceased they managed to cannibalize parts to get one truck going and set off for the rendezvous with Fraser, only to find nobody there."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ba7e2caa-63db-3f45-abb6-204972b075ba",
                        "entry_id": "158e6575-269a-34aa-96e2-589309e4772e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To reduce sales or market share (for one of one's own products) by introducing another."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "UK",
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8815b255-e9e9-4db4-b45b-e401834abade",
                                "sense_id": "ba7e2caa-63db-3f45-abb6-204972b075ba",
                                "text": "iPad mini to cannibalize 1M full-size iPad sales."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4a215407-2964-333e-8f8d-659bd123708b",
                        "entry_id": "158e6575-269a-34aa-96e2-589309e4772e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Rework old material; rehash."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "UK"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "18587eff-16bd-4acd-bdce-323db7a34375",
                                "sense_id": "4a215407-2964-333e-8f8d-659bd123708b",
                                "text": "When the album succeeds, such as on the swaggering, Queen-esque “Nothing’s Gonna Stop Us,” it does so on The Darkness’ own terms—that is, as a random ’80s-cliché generator. But with so many tired, lazy callbacks to its own threadbare catalog (including “Love Is Not The Answer,” a watery echo of the epic “I Believe In A Thing Called Love” from 2003’s Permission To Land), Hot Cakes marks the point where The Darkness has stopped cannibalizing the golden age of stadium rock and simply started cannibalizing itself. And, despite Hawkins’ inveterate crotch-grabbing, there was never that much meat there to begin with."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "cb1b04c4-1cdf-4021-aa62-22ce605adf78",
                        "source_entry_id": "158e6575-269a-34aa-96e2-589309e4772e",
                        "source_sense_description": "to eat one's own species",
                        "target_lang_word": "canibalizar",
                        "target_lang_code": "es",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "canibalizar",
                                "target_lang_code": "es",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4f37683d-8dd7-3adc-b53b-4a434954bdbd",
                                        "entry_id": "eacb2e8a-b83f-3692-873c-37de7f804d41",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Quitar partes a una máquina, generalmente ya fuera de servicio, para aprovecharlas con otros fines."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "99953518-b2a0-4362-affb-e413850e6117",
                                                "sense_id": "4f37683d-8dd7-3adc-b53b-4a434954bdbd",
                                                "text": "En el Perú y en otros países de América se usa el verbo canibalizar con el sentido de «desmantelar, desarmar una máquina para aprovechar sus piezas, como repuestos, en otras máquinas semejantes»."
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "57054ef3-4fc1-3bfd-bbeb-d19042f69d7a",
                                        "entry_id": "eacb2e8a-b83f-3692-873c-37de7f804d41",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Usar, sin autorización y generalmente con descuido, partes de un artículo, marca, texto u objeto protegido por derechos de autor."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "12ea0a04-af52-4e1f-bc48-80c5d0f919f8",
                                                "sense_id": "57054ef3-4fc1-3bfd-bbeb-d19042f69d7a",
                                                "text": "Frecuentemente, para designar el verbo «adaptar», se usan sinónimos como reproducir, imitar, duplicar, y hasta robar, destrozar, saquear, usurpar, canibalizar y violar un texto literario, metáforas con evidentes connotaciones de desprecio."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cfb3f689-f897-46cf-82c7-2cf5d13b2443",
                                                "sense_id": "57054ef3-4fc1-3bfd-bbeb-d19042f69d7a",
                                                "text": "Será necesario proceder a crear una versión reducida del producto actual que permita acceder a ese nuevo mercado potencial sin necesidad de canibalizar el producto en sí."
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"2\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
